e wave can terminate after ~30000. The wave (if any) therefore ends more than 4000 units before the route begins, so the two phenomena are not temporally coupled and the compound mechanism is absent."}, "raw_final_response": "**Findings**\n\n*Part 2 (route) \u2014 holds.* A time-respecting path 667\u2192734\u2192449\u21921188\u2192731 exists, and all four hops fall in a narrow late band: 667\u2192734 in (34100, 34250] (step_25, step_30), 734\u2192449 in (34250, 34400] (step_26, step_31), 449\u21921188 in (34400, 34700] (step_23, step_27), 1188\u2192731 in (34700, 34960] (step_24, step_28, step_20). Consecutive gaps are all well under 600. Route start \u2248 34.1\u201334.25k.\n\n*Part 1 (closure wave) \u2014 at best early, and not temporally coupled.* The 12-node group carries 4 static triangles (12 incidences, 1/node \u2014 step_04), but these are ignoring time. The group's activity is concentrated early: 15 / 13 / 9 events in [18400,22000] / [22000,26000] / [26000,30000], versus only 1 event in [30000,32000] and 6 in [32000,34000], and **zero** in [34000,34400] (step_29). Crucially, no triangle among these nodes has all three edges inside [32000,34000] (step_32), and a \u2264800-unit closure needs all three edges packed in an ~800 span \u2014 impossible in [30000,32000] (a single event). So the last admissible closing interaction cannot be later than ~30000, i.e. \u2265 ~4100 time units before the route begins, exceeding the 4000-unit admissible lag.\n\n*Confounder controls.* Aggregate volume is high (3164 events, 1682 active nodes \u2014 step_01) and a static 667\u2192731 connection exists via 734/449/1188 across the whole window (step_05\u2013step_11), but those are exactly the \"ignore time\" signals the task warns against; the decisive test is the wave-end\u2192route-start lag, which fails.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_f99874ad\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"compound\",\n  \"entities\": [12, 17, 34, 64, 169, 209, 304, 323, 331, 369, 40